  "summary": "The experiment tested a multimodal model combining scvi_n200 RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l image encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion, achieving validation accuracy of 0.7250 (F1: 0.6847), surpassing the best RNA-only configuration (0.6530). This suggests potential benefits from integrating high-quality image data with weighted fusion, though the exact contribution of the image encoder or fusion method remains uncertain without further comparison. The interaction between modalities and other factors like aggregation may also influence performance, warranting additional experiments."
